/// Whether this placement is the student's main one for the year.
///
/// `PRIMARY` is the only kind Phase 4 creates. `SECONDARY` exists for NEP
/// multidisciplinary enrolment and `EXCHANGE` for visiting placements; both are
/// declared now because the partial unique index that limits a student to one
/// live `PRIMARY` per year has to name the kind it applies to, and a value added
/// later would silently widen an index that already exists.
enum EnrollmentKind {
  PRIMARY
  SECONDARY
  EXCHANGE
}

/// The life of one academic-year placement.
///
/// Deliberately **without** `SUSPENDED`. Suspension is a property of the human,
/// not of the placement: a suspended student still occupies their seat in 9-A,
/// and duplicating the state here would leave two aggregates disagreeing about
/// the same fact. A whole year away is `ON_BREAK` on the enrolment plus
/// `ON_HOLD` on the admission.
enum EnrollmentStatus {
  /// Created, not yet in effect.
  PENDING
  /// The current placement.
  ACTIVE
  /// Paused for the year; the seat is retained.
  ON_BREAK
  /// Finished the year and moved up. Historical.
  PROMOTED
  /// Finished the year and repeats it. Historical.
  DETAINED
  /// Finished a terminal year. Historical.
  COMPLETED
  /// Placement moved elsewhere. Historical.
  TRANSFERRED
  /// The student left mid-year. Historical.
  DROPPED_OUT
  /// Voided. Historical.
  CANCELLED
  /// Replaced by a corrected row, which names this one. Historical.
  SUPERSEDED
}

/// Why this placement row exists.
///
/// Recorded rather than inferred. Timestamps cannot tell a correction from a
/// genuine mid-year move, and that is exactly the question asked when a
/// registrar is challenged about a student appearing in two classes.
enum EnrollmentOriginType {
  /// The first placement, written by `admit()`.
  ADMISSION
  /// Next year, next level.
  PROMOTION
  /// Next year, same level.
  REPEAT
  /// An operator's mistake, put right.
  CORRECTION
  /// A real mid-year move within the branch.
  TRANSFER
  /// A new spell of study for a returning student.
  READMISSION
  /// Imported from a previous system.
  MIGRATION
}

/// How the academic year ended for this placement.
///
/// **Enrollment owns the column; Examination owns the decision** (INV-ENR-013).
/// Nothing in this module writes it, and there is no route that can.
///
/// Three values, not a grading vocabulary. The blueprint specifies the column
/// but not its domain, so this carries only what the placement lifecycle itself
/// already distinguishes — `PASS` leads to `PROMOTED` or `COMPLETED`, `FAIL` to
/// `DETAINED`, and `WITHHELD` to neither yet. A richer result vocabulary
/// (grades, divisions, subject-wise outcomes) belongs to Examination's own
/// tables, not here.
enum EnrollmentResultOutcome {
  PASS
  FAIL
  WITHHELD
}
